[71.850524, "o", "Done — stopping here as requested. Summary of the actual result:\r\n\r\n## App: Orbit Desk (`orbit-desk.xdc`, 4.3 KB)\r\n- **Contents verified by ZIP listing:** only `index.html` (11.4 KB) and `manifest.toml` at the ZIP root; `webxdc.js` is **not** bundled. Package integrity checked (`testzip` clean).\r\n- **Features built:** three fictional missions (Helios-9 Solar Scout, Aurora Cargo Runner, Tidal-3 Research Dock), status filter chips (All / Launching / En route / Docked), a live UTC desk clock, and an interactive check-in button per mission.\r\n- **Dark navy theme** via CSS custom properties with layered radial-gradient background; all HTML/CSS/JS local, no CDN or external fetch.\r\n- **Check-in behavior:** updates the UI immediately (button flips to \"✓ Checked in\", persists in `localStorage`) and calls `window.webxdc.sendUpdate({payload: {event:\"checkin\", ...}})` when webxdc is available; a `setUpdateListener` merges check-ins from chat peers and never double-counts your own.\r\n\r\n## Sigma delivery (v0.2.0 at `/usr/local/bin/sigma`)\r\n- Fresh bot account created via `sigma init` (default name **Sigma**), address `[demo address redacted]`.\r\n- Connected to the invitation with alias **`me`** — the invitation was read from `invite.txt` into **argv only** by a Python subprocess, never echoed; raw stdout/stderr captured to private logs under `.private/` (which also excludes the invitation from what I printed). Handshake succeeded, returned contact ID **10**.\r\n- Sent `orbit-desk.xdc` to alias `me` via `send-webxdc --json`; core accepted it with `type: sent`.\r\n\r\n## Returned IDs (`result.json`, no invitation included)\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"app\": \"orbit-desk.xdc\",\r\n  \"alias\": \"me\",\r\n  \"contact_id\": 10,\r\n  \"chat_id\": 10,\r\n  \"message_id\": 16,\r\n  \"status\": \"sent\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\nNo other files or messages were sent, and the installed skill was left untouched. Note that `status: sent` reflects successful submission by the bot; SMTP submission doesn't itself confirm the recipient opened the message — the inviter just needs to receive the app in their chat.\r\n"]
